      ],
      "observed": "D3 is a 12 V zener connected with its cathode (pin 1, K) to GND and its anode (pin 2, A) to the T3 gate net /G_RPP. R7 pulls /G_RPP to T3 source (/+24V_F), so with a 24 V input D3 is forward-biased and clamps the gate to about 0.7 V above ground, giving VGS approximately -23.3 V for the P-channel AON6407.",
      "expected": "For the high-side P-channel reverse-polarity/load switch, the 12 V zener should be oriented to clamp the gate near +12 V relative to ground (cathode to /G_RPP/gate, anode to GND) or otherwise limit VGS to within the device rating, about -12 V when 24 V is present.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"47\") (name \"/G_{RPP}\") ... (node (ref \"D3\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") ... (node (ref \"T3\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"G\") ..."
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"76\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"D3\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"K\") ..."
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"6\") (name \"/+24V_{F}\") ... (node (ref \"T3\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"S\") ..."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "The PCB includes \"reverse polarity protection, TVS diodes, proper isolation\""
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The T3 gate-source voltage can exceed the AON6407 absolute maximum under normal 24 V operation, risking gate-oxide stress/failure and unreliable reverse-polarity protection.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows a reversed zener clamp on the high-side P-channel protection MOSFET T3, which can over-stress its gate-source voltage; other apparent mismatches seem to be documentation/reference numbering issues rather than connectivity faults."
}

